# JGDMS DER @Serializer registry -- PLATFORM-CONTROLLED, wire-contract (STD-006 §7.6.1).
#
# This is the SINGLE closed set of @Serializer(replaceObType=...) classes the DER
# codec (au.net.zeus.jgdms.der.serial.DerReplacer) will substitute for a
# non-@AtomicSerial value ON ENCODE, and admit as a nested field ON SCHEMA GENERATION.
# It is read from jgdms-der's OWN jar only (Class.getResourceAsStream, not a classpath
# getResources() merge) because the registered set is part of the wire contract: it
# feeds SchemaGenerator -> schemaDigest, so an addition -- especially an interface-keyed
# serializer -- is a versioned schema change requiring board review (STD-006 §7.6.1).
#
# NOTE (security review R2): this registry is an ENCODE-substitution + schema-generation
# determinism control. It is NOT a decode-admission boundary -- decode reconstructs any
# @AtomicSerial leaf the transmitted schema names regardless of this list; decode
# admission is enforced by ObjectCodec.admissibleConstructClass (declared-type gate) +
# the DeSerializationPermission("ATOMIC") gate + check(GetArg) + decode bounds.
#
# Each entry MUST be an @AtomicSerial + @Serializer class (DerReplacer refuses to
# register a non-@AtomicSerial one). One class name per line; '#' and blank lines
# ignored.
#
# X500Principal (a MethodConstraints principals[] element) is the only type a real
# constrained-proxy graph currently requires. Its wire form is getEncoded() carried
# VERBATIM (canonical ASN.1 DER of the DN); it must not be re-canonicalized/sorted.
# URI, URL, File and StackTraceElement were added 2026-10-20 (maintainer decision; each an inert value
# rebuilt from a string or four plain fields, loading no class and running no code):
#   URI    - its string form, reparsed with new URI(String);
#   URL    - its external form, reparsed with new URL(null, String) (equals/hashCode of a URL can
#            do a name lookup: prefer URI in new protocols);
#   File   - its file: URI (File.toURI(), so a relative path is sent as an absolute one);
#   StackTraceElement - declaringClass, methodName, fileName, lineNumber (the loader and module
#            names are not carried). It has its own serializer, StackTraceElementValueSerializer,
#            because DerThrowableForm's frames use StackTraceElementSerializer directly.
# Throwable, Properties and MarshalledObject are DEFERRED (unresolved security/canonicality
# defects; MarshalledObject is dangerous by decision) and are deliberately NOT listed.
org.apache.river.api.io.X500PrincipalSerializer
org.apache.river.api.io.URISerializer
org.apache.river.api.io.URLSerializer
org.apache.river.api.io.FileSerializer
org.apache.river.api.io.StackTraceElementValueSerializer
